<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Souphanouvong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a>–<a href="/years/1995">1995</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Red Prince</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Souphanouvong was a Lao prince and communist leader, known as the Red Prince, half-brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souvanna-phouma">Souvanna Phouma</a>. Trained as an engineer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, he joined the Lao Issara in 1945 and then founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pathet-lao">Pathet Lao</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> backing, leading it through decades of civil war. When the monarchy was abolished in 1975 he became the first president of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, serving until 1991.</p></div>
